// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildNote > matches the snapshot for a high finding 1`] = `
"Links on this page go nowhere

Page: https://shop.example/menu

Why it matters:
Visitors who click hit a dead end, and search engines take broken links as a sign the site is neglected.

How to fix it:
Point each link at the page's current address, or remove it. When a page moved, add a 301 redirect from the old address.

Technical detail:
a sampled same-site a[href] ends in 4xx or 5xx. 401, 403, 429 and 503 with Retry-After are refusals: listed as could not check, never broken. A 200 page that says "not found" (a soft 404) is out of scope

Evidence:
https://shop.example/gone returned 404

Check: broken-links"
`;
